From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: skip function 2 without a probe error

The C6 exposes two SDIO functions and only function 1 carries the
network interface.  Returning -EINVAL for function 2 made the driver core
log "probe with driver esp32_sdio failed with error -22" on every boot
(#12).  -ENODEV declines the function silently.

---
diff --git a/sdio/esp_sdio.c b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -1243,7 +1243,8 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (func->num != 1) {
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/* Function 2 is not ours; -ENODEV keeps the driver core quiet. */
+		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
 	esp_info("ESP network device detected\n");
